---
/**
 * Theming: how one small config (brand, corners, body size) reaches every component, with
 * live previews that read the same CSS variables the customizer writes, then the colour
 * token groups from tokens/tokens.json. Swatches and samples follow the theme the page is in.
 */
import Docs from '../layouts/Docs.astro'
import PageHeader from '../components/PageHeader.astro'
import Chip from '../components/Chip.astro'
import { page } from '../nav'
import { colorGroups } from '../lib/tokens'
import { highlight } from '../lib/highlight'

const h2 = 'text-lg font-medium text-text-default'
const prose = 'text-base leading-6 text-text-muted'
const panel = 'rounded-2xl border border-border-subtle p-4 sm:p-5'

const ramp = ['50', '200', '300', '500', '600', '700', '900', '950']
const radii = ['xs', 'sm', 'md', 'lg', 'xl', '2xl']
const sizes = [
  { k: '2xs', use: 'Fine print' },
  { k: 'xs', use: 'Captions, axis labels' },
  { k: 'sm', use: 'Body: labels, controls, menus' },
  { k: 'base', use: 'Docs prose, card titles' },
  { k: 'lg', use: 'Section headings' },
  { k: 'xl', use: 'Figures' },
  { k: '2xl', use: 'Page titles' },
]

const snippets = await highlight([
  {
    id: 'file',
    label: 'Exported file',
    code: `import '@satin/ui/styles.css'
import './satin-theme.css' // from the customizer: Export → Download`,
  },
  {
    id: 'code',
    label: 'In code',
    code: `import { themeCss } from '@satin/ui'

// Inject once, e.g. in a <style> in your root layout.
const css = themeCss({ brand: '#E5533D', radius: 1.5, fontSize: 14 })`,
  },
])
---

<Docs current="theming">
  <PageHeader id="theming" title={page('theming').title} description={page('theming').description} />

  <section aria-labelledby="how-title" class="flex flex-col gap-3 pt-6">
    <h2 id="how-title" class={h2}>How theming works</h2>
    <p class={prose}>
      Satin's tokens come in three layers. <strong class="font-medium text-text-default">Primitives</strong> are raw colours and
      sizes. <strong class="font-medium text-text-default">Semantic tokens</strong> give them a job, like
      <Chip>action/primary-bg</Chip> or <Chip>text/muted</Chip>, once for Light and once for Dark.{' '}
      <strong class="font-medium text-text-default">Components</strong> only ever read semantic tokens, never a raw value.
    </p>
    <p class={prose}>
      So a theme doesn't touch components at all. It repoints a few primitives and scales, and everything that reads them
      follows: buttons, focus rings, checkboxes, tones, charts. Try it with the customizer at the bottom of the page; every
      sample here reads the same variables.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="brand-title" class="flex flex-col gap-3 pt-10">
    <h2 id="brand-title" class={h2}>Brand</h2>
    <p class={prose}>
      One colour becomes the whole brand ramp. Each step keeps the lightness of Satin's own ramp, takes your hue and scales
      its chroma in OKLCH, so tints, borders and soft tones land where they did. The fills a button is painted with move to
      your colour's lightness, and the text on them turns dark when white would read under 4.5:1.
    </p>
    <div class={panel}>
      <ul class="grid grid-cols-4 gap-2 sm:grid-cols-8" aria-label="Brand ramp">
        {
          ramp.map((s) => (
            <li class="flex flex-col gap-1.5">
              <span class="h-10 rounded-md border border-border-subtle" style={`background:var(--color-blue-${s})`} />
              <span class="text-xs text-text-muted">{s}</span>
            </li>
          ))
        }
      </ul>
      <div class="mt-4 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-3 border-t border-border-subtle pt-4">
        <span class="inline-flex h-8 items-center rounded-lg bg-action-primary-bg px-3 text-sm font-medium text-action-primary-fg">Primary</span>
        <span data-tone="brand" class="inline-flex items-center rounded-sm bg-tone-bg px-2 py-1 text-sm font-medium text-tone-fg">Brand tone</span>
        <span class="inline-flex h-8 items-center rounded-lg border border-border-default px-3 text-sm text-text-default shadow-border-focus">Focus ring</span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="corners-title" class="flex flex-col gap-3 pt-10">
    <h2 id="corners-title" class={h2}>Corners</h2>
    <p class={prose}>
      One number scales every corner token: 0 is square, 1 is Satin's own, 1.5 is softer. Pills and circles stay round
      whatever the scale.
    </p>
    <ul class:list={[panel, 'grid grid-cols-3 gap-4 sm:grid-cols-6']} aria-label="Corner tokens">
      {
        radii.map((r) => (
          <li class="flex flex-col gap-2">
            <span class="aspect-square w-full border border-border-default bg-bg-muted" style={`border-radius:var(--radius-${r})`} />
            <Chip>radius-{r}</Chip>
          </li>
        ))
      }
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="type-title" class="flex flex-col gap-3 pt-10">
    <h2 id="type-title" class={h2}>Body text</h2>
    <p class={prose}>
      The body size is 13 or 14. The rest of the scale keeps its steps from it, so captions, headings and figures stay in
      proportion: at 13 it runs 10, 12, 13, 14, 16, 20, 24.
    </p>
    <ul class:list={[panel, 'flex flex-col divide-y divide-border-subtle py-1 sm:py-1']} aria-label="Type scale">
      {
        sizes.map(({ k, use }) => (
          <li class="flex items-baseline gap-4 py-2.5">
            <span class="w-14 shrink-0">
              <Chip>{k}</Chip>
            </span>
            <span class="min-w-0 flex-1 truncate text-text-default" style={`font-size:var(--text-${k})`}>
              {use}
            </span>
          </li>
        ))
      }
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="code-title" class="flex flex-col gap-3 pt-10">
    <h2 id="code-title" class={h2}>Use it in your app</h2>
    <p class={prose}>
      The theme is a short stylesheet of variables. Export it from the customizer and load it after Satin's styles, or build
      it in code from the same three values with <Chip>themeCss</Chip>.
    </p>
    {
      ['file', 'code'].map((id) => (
        <div class="overflow-hidden rounded-2xl border border-border-subtle bg-bg-field">
          <div class="code-block overflow-x-auto py-3" set:html={snippets[id]} />
        </div>
      ))
    }
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="tokens-title" class="flex flex-col gap-3 pt-10">
    <h2 id="tokens-title" class={h2}>Tokens</h2>
    <p class={prose}>Every semantic colour by group, in Light and Dark, straight from tokens.json.</p>
    <ul class="grid grid-cols-1 gap-3 sm:grid-cols-2">
      {
        colorGroups.map((g) => (
          <li>
            <a
              href={`/theming/${g.role}`}
              class="flex h-full flex-col gap-4 rounded-xl border border-border-subtle p-4 transition-colors duration-(--duration-fast) ease-(--ease-out) hover:bg-bg-hover focus-visible:shadow-border-focus focus-visible:outline-none"
            >
              <span aria-hidden class="flex">
                {g.tokens.slice(0, 8).map((t) => (
                  <span
                    class="-mr-1.5 size-6 shrink-0 rounded-full border border-border-default ring-2 ring-bg-card"
                    style={`background:var(${t.css})`}
                  />
                ))}
              </span>
              <span class="flex flex-col gap-0.5">
                <span class="flex items-baseline justify-between gap-2">
                  <span class="text-base font-medium text-text-default">{g.title}</span>
                  <span class="text-sm text-text-muted">{g.tokens.length} tokens</span>
                </span>
                <span class="text-base leading-6 text-text-muted">{g.description}</span>
              </span>
            </a>
          </li>
        ))
      }
    </ul>
  </section>
</Docs>
